{
 "_doc": "Heracles (GAME_DESIGN.md: Heroes; art style test, owner request 10/31/2026, second version after the owner's feedback). Pixel art as rows of letters, 1 letter = 1 pixel, drawn facing right; the game mirrors it to face left. '.' is transparent; every other letter is a colour from palette. Frames: idle, and walk (played in turn while moving). anchor is the pixel under the middle of the feet. Iconography from Greek vase painting and Pseudo-Apollodorus (Bibliotheca 2.5.1): the Nemean lion's skin worn as a hood (its head over his) and cloak, its paws knotted at the throat; a beard; a short chiton; sandals; and his club. Drawn by scratchpad tool build_heracles.py (shapes, then an automatic dark outline).",
